@baseUrl = http://localhost:5048

# ConferenceProFlow — M4.2D3: Jaeger end-to-end demonstration.
# Local development only; never use real participant personal data.
# If Registration API listens on a different URL, update ONLY @baseUrl.
# Execute requests 01 and 02; STOP and provision the new session inventory
# with docs/OBSERVABILITY_E2E_SEED.sql before executing requests 03-08.
# Named HTTP responses automatically supply all IDs; do not type GUIDs here.
# Use a NEW session for every run. Never reset existing data to rerun this demo.

### 01 — Create dedicated observability demonstration conference
# @name obsCreateConference
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conferences
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "ConferenceProFlow Observability E2E Demo 2027",
  "startsAtUtc": "2027-06-01T08:00:00Z",
  "endsAtUtc": "2027-06-02T18:00:00Z"
}

### 02 — Create fresh session (COPY its response `id` ONCE into SQL seed/checks)
# @name obsCreateSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conferences/{{obsCreateConference.response.body.$.id}}/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Tracing Durable Messages with RabbitMQ and Kafka",
  "startsAtUtc": "2027-06-01T10:00:00Z",
  "endsAtUtc": "2027-06-01T11:30:00Z"
}

### STOP HERE — Run docs/OBSERVABILITY_E2E_SEED.sql with session id from 02.
### 03 — Create synthetic participant Olivia Bennett
# @name obsCreateParticipant1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Olivia Bennett",
  "email": "olivia.bennett.m42d3.{{$guid}}@example.com"
}

### 04 — Register Olivia
# @name obsCreateRegistration1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantId": "{{obsCreateParticipant1.response.body.$.id}}",
  "sessionId": "{{obsCreateSession.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 05 — Create synthetic participant Noah Brooks
# @name obsCreateParticipant2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Noah Brooks",
  "email": "noah.brooks.m42d3.{{$guid}}@example.com"
}

### 06 — Register Noah
# @name obsCreateRegistration2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantId": "{{obsCreateParticipant2.response.body.$.id}}",
  "sessionId": "{{obsCreateSession.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 07 — Create synthetic participant Sophie Chen
# @name obsCreateParticipant3
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Sophie Chen",
  "email": "sophie.chen.m42d3.{{$guid}}@example.com"
}

### 08 — Register Sophie
# @name obsCreateRegistration3
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantId": "{{obsCreateParticipant3.response.body.$.id}}",
  "sessionId": "{{obsCreateSession.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 09 — Read Olivia's latest status (repeat only GET while Pending)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/{{obsCreateRegistration1.response.body.$.id}}

### 10 — Read Noah's latest status (repeat only GET while Pending)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/{{obsCreateRegistration2.response.body.$.id}}

### 11 — Read Sophie's latest status (repeat only GET while Pending)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/{{obsCreateRegistration3.response.body.$.id}}

# Expected for this fresh session after asynchronous processing:
#   Two Confirmed, one Rejected, zero Pending (order is not guaranteed).
# Do NOT re-run POST registrations to fix a Pending status.
